Arctic Prime CSS Color Restore Task

Update "Main.css" to restore the colorful Aetherion cyber style, but do it carefully and only change colors/theme values.

Do NOT change:

- layout
- sizing
- spacing
- padding
- widths/heights
- FXML
- Java files
- project structure

Only adjust CSS colors, gradients, borders, glow, and readability.

Use this color direction:

- main background: very dark space blue / near black
- panels: dark blue-black gradient
- primary accent: cyan / teal
- secondary accent: amber / orange
- success accent: neon green
- warning/error accent: red/pink
- main text: soft cyan-white
- muted text: blue-gray

Suggested palette:

- Background: "#05080f", "#0b1017", "#08111d"
- Panel: "#10263d", "#08111d"
- Cyan: "#00d9ff", "#00efd8"
- Green: "#00ff95", "#23c698"
- Amber: "#ff9f1c", "#ffcf66"
- Red: "#ff4b5c", "#ffd6d6"
- Text: "#d7f8ff"
- Muted text: "#9fc2d6"

Make these areas more colorful again:

- ".app-root"
- ".top-bar"
- ".footer-bar"
- ".sidebar"
- ".right-rail"
- ".section-header"
- ".control-card"
- ".ai-command-panel"
- ".rail-panel"
- ".primary-button"
- ".danger-button"
- ".nav-button"
- ".status-pill-green"
- ".status-pill-cyan"
- ".status-pill-amber"
- ".progress-bar .bar"
- ".scroll-bar .thumb"

Important:
Keep text readable.
No white JavaFX default boxes.
No massive visual overhaul.
No layout movement.

Goal:
Restore the Aetherion colorful cyber look while keeping the current structure stable.